Task-Aware Object Selection Using FPGA-Based Two-Stage Approximation

Team Name : ChipUp
Team ID   : 188
Institution: Chennai Institute of Technology - Anna University

======================================================================
OVERVIEW
======================================================================

This project implements a hardware accelerator for task-aware object
selection using an FPGA-based two-stage approximation pipeline.

The hardware receives candidate objects from the Stage 1 software
pipeline and performs task-aware ranking using RTL modules. It computes
task-aware scores (Score1 = Confidence x Task Relevance), filters
low-priority objects using a configurable threshold, selects the best
two candidate objects, and stores the results through an AXI4 Master
interface.

The complete RTL design has been functionally verified using QuestaSim.
RTL synthesis has been completed using Xilinx Vivado 2018.2.

======================================================================
PROJECT FILES
======================================================================

top_module.v            - Top-level RTL module
top2_comparator.v       - Score computation and object selection
axi_slave_interface.v   - AXI4 Slave interface
axi_master_interface.v  - AXI4 Master interface
memory_model.v          - Simulation-only AXI memory model
testbench.v             - Functional verification testbench
Makefile                - QuestaSim simulation automation
Makefile_Vivado         - Vivado synthesis automation
run_vivado.tcl          - Vivado Tcl synthesis script
README                  - This file

======================================================================
RTL MODULE DESCRIPTION
======================================================================

1. top_module.v
   Top-level module integrating all RTL components.

2. top2_comparator.v
   - Computes task-aware score: Score1 = Confidence x Task Relevance
   - Filters objects below the configured threshold
   - Selects the Primary and Alternative candidate objects
   - Uses DSP48E1 blocks for efficient multiply operations

3. axi_slave_interface.v
   Implements the AXI4 Slave interface.
   Functions:
   - Receives object confidence values from the host
   - Receives task relevance weights from the host
   - Accepts start command to initiate hardware processing
   - Returns processed results to the host

4. axi_master_interface.v
   Implements the AXI4 Master interface.
   - Writes computed results into memory after processing completes
   - Implements 8-state FSM: IDLE, WR_ADDR_1/2, WR_DATA_1/2,
     WR_RESP_1/2, DONE

5. memory_model.v
   Simulation-only AXI memory model.
   Used only for functional verification in QuestaSim.
   Not included in FPGA synthesis.

6. testbench.v
   Verifies:
   - Score computation (Score1 = Confidence x Task Relevance)
   - Threshold filtering
   - Primary object selection
   - Alternative object selection
   - AXI read/write transactions
   - Displays PASS/FAIL summary after simulation

======================================================================
HARDWARE PIPELINE
======================================================================

   AXI4 Slave Interface
          |
          v
   Top-2 Comparator (Score1 = Confidence x Task Relevance)
          |
          v
   AXI4 Master Interface
          |
          v
   Memory Model (Simulation only)

======================================================================
SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS
======================================================================

- QuestaSim (for RTL simulation)
- Xilinx Vivado 2018.2 (for RTL synthesis)
- GNU Make / mingw32-make (Windows)

======================================================================
COMPILATION (QuestaSim)
======================================================================

1. Extract the project files.

2. Open Command Prompt in the project directory.

3. Run:

      # Windows (MinGW/MSYS):
      mingw32-make -f Makefile_Questa compile

      # Linux / macOS:
      make -f Makefile_Questa compile

   This command:
   - Creates the required work library
   - Maps the work library
   - Compiles all RTL source files
   - Compiles the testbench

   Successful compilation ends with:
      Errors: 0
      Warnings: 0

======================================================================
SIMULATION (QuestaSim)
======================================================================

1. Open QuestaSim.

2. Change working directory to the project folder:

      cd <project_directory>

3. Load the testbench:

      vsim -voptargs="+acc" work.testbench

4. Run the simulation:

      run 20us

   The testbench executes $finish at the end of simulation.
   Select "No" in the confirmation dialog to keep the waveform open
   for inspection.

======================================================================
VIVADO SYNTHESIS
======================================================================

Target Device : xc7k70tfbv676-1 (Kintex-7)
Tool          : Xilinx Vivado 2018.2

To synthesize the RTL:

1. Open Command Prompt in the project directory.

2. Run either:

      mingw32-make -f Makefile_Vivado     (Windows)

   or directly:

      vivado -mode batch -source run_vivado.tcl

   This generates:
   - utilization_report.txt
   - timing_report.txt

Note: memory_model.v and testbench.v are excluded from synthesis.

